    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n68 Victoria Place is an exceptionally appealing three-bedroom, three-bathroom semi-detached family residence, superbly positioned on a most attractive extra-large end site within a quiet and well-regarded enclave, just moments from the town centre and a wide range of everyday amenities. \n\nBuilt in 2004 and extending to approximately 96 square metres / 1,033 square feet, this beautifully presented home offers a rare combination of stylish interiors, generous outdoor space, excellent privacy and highly versatile additional accommodation, making it a property that is sure to attract significant interest from families, first-time buyers, downsizers and those seeking a home with superb work-from-home or guest accommodation potential.\n\nFrom the moment one arrives, the property makes a strong impression. The end-site setting provides a wonderful sense of space, while the south-facing landscaped gardens and patio areas create a bright, sheltered and highly usable outdoor environment. The gardens have been thoughtfully maintained with mature planting, attractive fencing, paved seating areas and excellent privacy, offering the perfect setting for outdoor dining, summer relaxation or safe family enjoyment. The site also benefits from numerous storage sheds, a covered outdoor area and a detached outbuilding, adding tremendous practicality and flexibility rarely found in a home of this type.\n\nInternally, number 68 is warm, inviting and full of character. The welcoming entrance hall leads through to Kitchen / Dining and onto a bright and comfortable living room, where high-gloss timber flooring, recessed lighting and a striking feature media wall combine to create a stylish yet homely space. The living area enjoys a lovely flow through to the kitchen and dining area, making the ground floor ideal for both everyday family life and entertaining. The fitted kitchen is bright and functional, with generous storage, tiled flooring, ample worktop space and direct access to the rear garden, allowing the interior and exterior living spaces to connect with ease. A guest WC completes the ground floor accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, the property continues to impress with three well-proportioned bedrooms, each offering a bright and comfortable setting. The principal bedroom benefits from built-in wardrobes and an en-suite shower room, while the additional bedrooms are ideally suited for children, guests or home office use. The main bathroom has been upgraded in a contemporary style and features attractive tiling, a curved shower enclosure, modern sanitary ware and a chrome heated towel rail, giving the first floor a fresh and polished finish. A bright landing area enhances the sense of space and light throughout the upper level.\n\nOne of the outstanding features of this property is the detached outbuilding to the rear, which doubles as a utility room and second living room. This highly valuable space offers an excellent range of possible uses, whether as a family den, home office, guest overflow area, hobby room, gym space or practical laundry and storage zone. With its own fitted units, seating area and generous proportions, it significantly enhances the overall usability of the property and sets 68 Victoria Place apart from many comparable homes.\n\nWith a BER rating of B, this residence offers comfortable modern living in a convenient and mature setting. Its combination of three bedrooms, three bathrooms, excellent presentation, south-facing gardens, extra-large end site and versatile detached outbuilding makes it a truly special home. Convenient to the town centre, local services, shops, schools and amenities, 68 Victoria Place is a beautifully maintained and highly desirable dwelling that offers far more than first meets the eye."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
